# DTF tier manifest: conda-repodata-revision  (artifact-keeper#4174, epic
#   #4172, tier named in #4188)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE BUG (1.11.x)
# #4174  every hosted `repodata.json`, `.zst`, `.bz2`, `current_repodata.json`
#        and JLAP request listed the whole repository (every row with its
#        metadata JSON) and re-rendered and re-compressed the subdir: N
#        installers refreshing one channel cost N full renders, and a warm
#        request on a 30,000-record subdir cost as much as a cold one.
#
# THE FIX (1.12.0, artifact-keeper G5 PR1 and PR2)
#        a subdir's documents are rendered once per revision (bumped by every
#        upload, withdrawal, delete and quarantine change) and kept; concurrent
#        cold requests share one render, counted by
#        ak_repo_metadata_regenerations_total{format="conda",scope="subdir"}.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   SQL seed (slot Postgres): one hosted channel, 3,000 names x 10 versions
#     (30,000 noarch rows) with conda metadata
#   PUT    /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}        one real upload (build.sh)
#   GET    /conda/{hosted}/noarch/repodata.json.zst  x24 concurrent, cold
#   GET    /api/v1/admin/metrics                Prometheus text
#   DELETE /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}        withdraw
#   every encoding decoded by fixtures/repodata_check.py (python:3.14-slim)
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1): see oracle.sh's header.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: bursts of concurrent repodata requests.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
